{%- comment -%}
  Outputs the theme-asset URL of a product's background-free cutout, or
  nothing if that product has no cutout. Nothing else — so callers can do:

    {%- capture cutout -%}{%- render 'gpod-cutout-url', handle: p.handle -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if cutout != blank -%} ... {%- endif -%}

  Why an explicit allow-list rather than just building the filename: an
  `asset_url` for a file that is not in the theme resolves to a URL that 404s,
  silently, as a broken image. The list is the only thing that knows which of
  the catalogue actually has an asset.

  WHY THESE EXIST AT ALL: the product photo library has the marketing template
  — a vertical "THE GPOD [PRODUCT]" wordmark — baked into the pixels of every
  frame for 13 of 15 products. Background removal cuts around baked-in text
  and leaves a floating logo, so each cutout was cropped past the branding band
  first. See GPOD/Product-Cutouts/MANIFEST.md for the per-product provenance.

  The three monopods are stored ROTATED ~38°. Trimmed to their true silhouette
  they are 0.06-0.13 aspect — literal hairlines that vanish in any card. The
  angle is the same fix a reshoot would apply, done to the asset.

  These are theme assets rather than Shopify Files, so there is no CDN resize:
  each is pre-sized to 700px on the long edge, which is 2x the largest place
  they are used (an Explore card). If they ever need to render bigger than
  ~350px, move them to Files with a `gpod.cutout` file_reference metafield and
  use image_url — that is the upgrade path, not a bigger PNG here.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign cutout_handles = 'gpodmagsafe,gpodx,gpod-pauly-p2,gpod-travel-1,gpod-studio,gpod-mini,indoor-base-for-gpod-gpod-mini,connect,gpod-caddy,replacement-magnet-for-magsafe,gpod-gplate,gpod-pocket-g,g-bundle-one-gpod-with-gpod-base,g-bundle-two-gpod-x-with-gpod-base,g-bundle-three-gpod-pauly-p-and-gpod-base' | split: ','

  if cutout_handles contains handle
    assign cutout_file = 'gpod-cutout-' | append: handle | append: '.png'
    echo cutout_file | asset_url
  endif
-%}
